WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.853 --> 00:00:02.925
- [Narrator] Some people
associate instant noodles

00:00:02.925 --> 00:00:04.982
with broke college students,

00:00:04.982 --> 00:00:06.886
but instant ramen wasn't created

00:00:06.886 --> 00:00:09.630
for a bunch of hungry 20 year olds.

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:12.302
The man who invented them
was much more ambitious.

00:00:12.302 --> 00:00:16.699
He set out to solve a
hunger crisis in Japan.

00:00:16.699 --> 00:00:20.493
After World War II, food
shortages plagued Japanese cities,

00:00:20.493 --> 00:00:22.412
so the U.S. supplied wheat flour

00:00:22.412 --> 00:00:25.045
and encouraged the Japanese to make bread.

00:00:25.045 --> 00:00:27.815
One man named Momofuku Ando

00:00:27.815 --> 00:00:29.745
didn't understand why his
people would make bread

00:00:29.745 --> 00:00:32.743
instead of noodles, something
that was already part

00:00:32.743 --> 00:00:34.184
of their culture.

00:00:34.184 --> 00:00:36.633
Ando decided to take
matters into his own hands

00:00:36.633 --> 00:00:39.980
and create a new ramen made to last.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:41.479
He spent a year trying to figure out how

00:00:41.479 --> 00:00:43.786
to preserve the noodles.

00:00:43.786 --> 00:00:46.728
He needed a nonperishable,
tasty, and easy recipe,

00:00:46.728 --> 00:00:49.191
but it was a challenge to
maintain the robust flavors

00:00:49.191 --> 00:00:53.280
and unique texture that most
people were accustomed to.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:55.725
It wasn't until his wife
was making dinner one night

00:00:55.725 --> 00:00:59.354
and he threw some noodles
in a bowl of hot tempura oil

00:00:59.354 --> 00:01:01.456
that he realized flash frying the noodles

00:01:01.456 --> 00:01:03.722
was the answer he had been looking for.

00:01:03.722 --> 00:01:05.585
This method not only dehydrated them,

00:01:05.585 --> 00:01:08.105
it left small perforations
that allowed the noodles

00:01:08.105 --> 00:01:10.778
to recook quickly.

00:01:10.778 --> 00:01:12.726
And there you have it,
instant ramen noodles

00:01:12.726 --> 00:01:14.653
became an instant success.

00:01:14.653 --> 00:01:16.167
Ando's products gained notoriety

00:01:16.167 --> 00:01:19.390
when he introduced the
packaged ramen in the 1950s

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:22.009
and later Cup Noodles in 1978.

00:01:22.009 --> 00:01:23.430
His company began selling upwards

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:25.536
of 40 billion units every year,

00:01:25.536 --> 00:01:29.439
and Momofuku Ando became
a culinary icon in Japan.

00:01:29.439 --> 00:01:32.974
So, the next time you heat
up a cup of instant noodles,

00:01:32.974 --> 00:01:36.105
remember, you're slurping down
a little piece of history.

00:01:36.105 --> 00:01:39.855
(lively instrumental music)

